Select **G2:G201**.\n2. HOME → **Conditional Formatting ▾** → **Highlight Cells Rules** → **Duplicate Values…**.\n3. Keep **Duplicate** and **Light Red Fill with Dark Red Text** → **OK**.\n\nChecked: a Duplicate Values rule on G2:G201.","criteria":[{"rule":"sheet","path":"conditionalFormats","includes":{"range":"G2:G201","type":"duplicate","style":"lightRedDarkRed"}}]},{"n":5,"marks":2,"text":"With Conditional Formatting apply Blue Data Bars (Gradient Fill) to the Basic Pay column F2:F201.","solution":"1. Select **F2:F201**.\n2. HOME → **Conditional Formatting ▾** → **Data Bars** → Gradient Fill → **Blue Data Bar**.\n\nChecked: a blue Data Bars rule on F2:F201.","criteria":[{"rule":"sheet","path":"conditionalFormats","includes":{"range":"F2:F201","type":"dataBar","style":"blueBar"}}]},{"n":6,"marks":1,"text":"Insert a Comment on cell A1 with the text \"Unique ID\".","solution":"1. Right-click **A1** → **Insert Comment** (or REVIEW → **New Comment**).\n2. Type **Unique ID** and click outside the comment.\n\nChecked: A1 has the comment \"Unique ID\".","criteria":[{"rule":"cells","range":"A1","props":{"comment":["Unique ID"]}}]},{"n":7,"marks":1,"text":"Hide the Mobile No column G.","solution":"1. Right-click the column letter **G** → **Hide** (or HOME → **Format ▾** → Hide & Unhide → **Hide Columns**).\n\nChecked: column G is hidden.","criteria":[{"rule":"sheet","path":"hiddenCols","includes":6}]},{"n":8,"marks":1,"text":"Set the Row Height of the heading row (row 1) to 30.","solution":"1. Right-click the row number **1** → **Row Height…** (or HOME → **Format ▾** → **Row Height…**).\n2. Type **30** → **OK**.\n\nChecked: row 1 is 30 high.","criteria":[{"rule":"sheet","path":"rowHeights.1","equals":30}]},{"n":9,"marks":1,"text":"Set the Column Width of the Employee Name column B to 30.","solution":"1. Right-click the column letter **B** → **Column Width…** (or HOME → **Format ▾** → **Column Width…**).\n2. Type **30** → **OK**.\n\nChecked: column B is 30 wide.","criteria":[{"rule":"sheet","path":"colWidths.B","equals":30}]},{"n":10,"marks":2,"text":"Rotate the text of the heading row A1:O1 with Orientation → Angle Counterclockwise.","solution":"1. Select **A1:O1**.\n2. HOME → **Orientation (ab↗) ▾** → **Angle Counterclockwise**.\n\nChecked: every heading cell is turned 45°.","criteria":[{"rule":"cells","range":"A1:O1","props":{"rotate":[45]}}]},{"n":11,"marks":2,"text":"Set the page Margins to Narrow and center the sheet Horizontally on the page (PAGE LAYOUT → Margins → Custom Margins → Center on page).","solution":"1. PAGE LAYOUT → **Margins ▾** → **Narrow**.\n2. PAGE LAYOUT → **Margins ▾** → **Custom Margins…** → Center on page: tick **Horizontally** → **OK**.\n\nChecked: narrow margins, centred horizontally.","criteria":[{"rule":"sheet","path":"margins","equals":"Narrow"},{"rule":"sheet","path":"centerHorizontally","equals":true}]},{"n":12,"marks":1,"text":"With Scale to Fit set the Width to 1 page (PAGE LAYOUT tab), so the sheet prints one page wide.","solution":"1. PAGE LAYOUT → Scale to Fit group → **Width ▾** → **1 page**.\n\nChecked: the sheet is set to 1 page wide.","criteria":[{"rule":"sheet","path":"fitWidth","equals":1}]},{"n":13,"marks":2,"text":"Apply Double Underline to the heading row A1:O1.","solution":"1. Select **A1:O1**.\n2. HOME → **Underline ▾** → **Double Underline**.\n\nChecked: every heading cell has a double underline.","criteria":[{"rule":"cells","range":"A1:O1","props":{"underline":[true],"underlineStyle":["double"]}}]},{"n":14,"marks":2,"text":"With Data Validation allow only a Whole number between 15000 and 60000 in the Basic Pay column F2:F201.","solution":"1. Select **F2:F201**.\n2. DATA → **Data Validation**.\n3. Allow **Whole number**, Data **between**, Minimum **15000**, Maximum **60000** → **OK**.\n\nChecked: the validation rule on F2:F201.","criteria":[{"rule":"sheet","path":"validations","includes":{"range":"F2:F201","type":"whole","operator":"between","value1":"15000","value2":"60000"}}]},{"n":15,"marks":2,"text":"Freeze the First Column of the sheet (VIEW → Freeze Panes).","solution":"1. VIEW → **Freeze Panes ▾** → **Freeze First Column**.\n\nChecked: column A stays visible while scrolling right.","criteria":[{"rule":"sheet","path":"freeze","equals":"B1"}]}]